=== G2. RESAMPLING THE SALT WIDENS THE INTERVAL ===
  The broken mechanism held the salt fixed and resampled only the unit, so the
  salt's variance could not enter any interval. The term under test here is
  ANOTHER information-free draw -- a thing that is known to carry nothing, so the
  honest interval must contain zero and a mechanism that says otherwise is wrong.
  locus   conditional width   unconditional width   widened by   verdicts
  board             1.431                 2.438       1.70x   one-draw: RESOLVED BEATS FLOOR | distribution: not resolved
  QB                0.000                 0.915        nanx   one-draw: not resolved | distribution: not resolved
  RB                0.000                 0.663        nanx   one-draw: not resolved | distribution: not resolved
  WR                1.792                 2.535       1.42x   one-draw: not resolved | distribution: not resolved
  TE                1.559                 1.950       1.25x   one-draw: RESOLVED WORSE THAN FLOOR | distribution: not resolved

=== G9. WHAT IS THE REFEREE'S OWN FALSE-RESOLUTION RATE? ===
  Every draw is information-free, so judging draw j against the OTHER draws is a
  test whose null is TRUE. A rule reported as 5% that never fires is not a
  conservative 5% test -- it is a 0% test, and it cannot resolve anything.
  This is the check audible#86 and #87 never ran.
  locus  resolved/n     rate  beats  worse   ref-set p:   min    5th    50th
  board      0/ 40     0.0%      0      0            0.050  0.050  0.650
  QB         0/ 40     0.0%      0      0            0.050  0.100  0.700
  RB         0/ 40     0.0%      0      0            0.050  0.050  0.950
  WR         1/ 40     2.5%      0      1            0.050  0.050  0.550
  TE         0/ 40     0.0%      0      0            0.050  0.050  0.550

  smallest two-sided reference-set p attainable with K=40 draws: 0.0488
  K=24 bottoms out at 0.080 and CANNOT express a 5% test at any effect
  size. K=39 is the smallest that reaches 0.050. That is why K=40 is drawn here.

